        "description": "Four astronauts. One historic mission. \n \nJoin the four crew members embarking on Nasa's Artemis II mission, the first crewed journey to the moon in over fifty years. \n \nFrom training to take off, we see what it really takes to travel further from the earth than ever before. \n \nAs the astronauts return to the moon, watch as they witness a total solar eclipse from deep space, navigate the unglamorous realities of survival in orbit, and ultimately return home with a dramatic splashdown in the Pacific Ocean.\n \nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews \n \nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news \n \n#Space #Moon #BBCNews\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#BBCNews",
